  "id": "gambang_kromong",
  "name": "Gambang kromong (Betawi and Chinese-Indonesian ensemble)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Ensemble of the Betawi and Chinese-Indonesian (peranakan, Cina Benteng) communities of Jakarta and Tangerang, named for the gambang wooden xylophone (here the xylophone card) and the kromong row of small kettle gongs (here the bonang card). Chinese two-string fiddles (tehyan, kongahyan, sukong), suling (here the generic bamboo-flute card), kendang (here the generic hand-drum card), kecrek and gong complete it, playing an older Chinese-derived lagu dalem repertoire and the later lagu sayur songs for weddings and lenong theatre.",
